# Everything the build does not need. This is a security control as much as a
# speed one: whatever reaches the build context can end up in a layer, and a
# layer is readable by anyone who can pull the image. .env and .git are the two
# that matter -- v1's context included the whole working tree.

# Deny by default, then re-admit exactly what the build uses.
*

!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!src/
!data/corpus/
!docker/requirements-assistant.lock

# Re-exclude anything that could have slipped under the allowances above.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.env
**/.env.*
